<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanesh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kültepe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanesh, modern Kültepe in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, was an ancient city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. In the early second millennium BCE it hosted the most important Assyrian merchant colony, or karum. Thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> tablets found there document the trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> and textiles for Anatolian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> that underpinned early Assyrian power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanesh.jpg" alt="Kanesh" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Klaus-Peter Simon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%BCltepeOberstadtPalast.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
